# tree.manifest -- portable description of a Linux filesystem subtree for the runtimes
# Linux-leg walk tests (tests/unit/test_runtimes_linux_parsers.cpp materializes it onto
# disk under a yuzu_test_runtimes_ TempDir at run time; nothing here is tracked as real
# directories or symlinks, so a Windows checkout is unaffected).
#
# Line grammar (a blank line or a line starting '#' is ignored):
#   <relative-path> TAB <payload>
# payload:
#   T:<text>       regular file with that text (escapes: \n newline, \t tab, \\ backslash)
#   L:<target>     symlink to <target> (verbatim, may be relative or dangling)
#   D:             (empty) directory
#
# PROVENANCE (per-section labels; the directory-level provenance.txt holds the capture
# commands, images and dates for the release sources and the listings):
#   REAL CAPTURE     -- structure and names taken from a command-only Docker container
#   RECONSTRUCTION   -- a link kind or empty placeholder file content that the capture did
#                       not record; named as such
#
# -- JVM ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REAL CAPTURE: eclipse-temurin:17 -- /opt/java/openjdk/release (content: T: below, the
#   verbatim file as recorded in temurin17_release.txt).
# REAL CAPTURE: debian:bookworm + openjdk-17-jre-headless --
#   /usr/lib/jvm/java-17-openjdk-arm64/release (content: T: below, the verbatim file as
#   recorded in debian_openjdk17_release.txt).
# RECONSTRUCTION: java-1.17.0-openjdk-arm64 is recorded in provenance.txt as a second entry
#   for the same install; that it is a symlink to java-17-openjdk-arm64 is Debian packaging
#   behaviour, not something the capture listed.
